==Strategy==
With an enemy limit of 17 instead of just 2, this stage removes one of [[Filibuster Obstructa|Filibuster Obstructa]]'s weaknesses in the [[Filibuster Invasion (Cats of the Cosmos)|original stage]], allowing many more threats to be present simultaneously, which can be quite the handful given most of them have post-[[Immeasurable Power]] scaling (1.2x the magnifications used in [[Uncanny Legends]] and early [[Zero Legends]]).

The presence of UltraBaaBaa means you'll want at least one [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breaker]] so consider bringing [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kitty of Liberty]], who also has a good range and attack power to deal chip damage to the Ostromeda present. In some strategies, UltraBaaBaa is used as a stepping stone to stack piercing attackers like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]].

The [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] is recommended to inflict large amounts of damage to [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] and can be the difference between victory or defeat.

That leaves Filibuster himself, who is unchanged aside from a 200% magnification to prevent him from dying too quickly. The stage length is as wide as it is in [[A Whole New World]], which means pinning him at the enemy base allows the [[Cat Base]] to avoid his attack. This will be your primary goal throughout the entire stage. However, the periodic spawns of powerful enemies and waves of Zollows will inevitably push you back, so always be prepared for these threats. You'll want to quickly Z-Kill Deathshund via [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]], [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Island Cat]], or any options which outrange him, then make sure Filibuster is pinned at his base before Ostromeda spawns. Taking out Ostromeda wouldn't be easy, even with their exploitable [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] trait, especially when Dread Bore enters play. Lure both Ostromeda and Dread Bore to your base after Filibuster gets his first attack off, and do whatever you can to dispatch them before Filibuster fully charges his second attack, this time likely in range to destroy your base. If done correctly, the only threat left will be Lord Gravey, who cannot push much on his own due to his backswing.

Use any means you can to push Lord Gravey back with Filibuster, optimally using [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|units with the Knockback ability]]. Units like [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] are great for this stage, as well as [[Good-Luck Ebisu (Super Rare Cat)|Bad-Luck Ebisu]] due to his ability to Knockback enemies as well as inflict other debuffs.

As Filibuster Obstructa was released far before the introduction of [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge units]] and was never given a retroactive immunity to either them or [[Explosion|Explosions]], the use of such units is advised. If they spawn in the right place at the right time, they can easily interrupt Filibuster's foreswing, even if other nasty enemies are in the way.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]]: One of the better picks for this stage, as her [[Long Distance]] attacks can reach Filibuster if he's slightly behind other threats, and her [[Surge Attack|Surges]] can constantly force him to reposition due to their high damage, being capable of juggling the peons and quickly killing Zollow before he even gets to attack. Her Curse ability can also shut down Shibalien Elite and Ostromeda's Warp as well as Lord Gravey's Knockback. She should be ideally sent as soon as the first Deathshund is Z-Killed so another replacement can be fielded by the time Filibuster manages to get an attack off.
*[[Bliza (Uber Rare Cat)|Blizarena]]: A midranged tank with Resistance against Aliens/Zombies, Blizarena does surprisingly well here, as she also has Zombie Killer and is Immune to Warp/Toxic, both of which allow her to simply tank most of the threats here. If she ever falls, a replacement is likely to be ready soon. Her 100% Barrier Breaker and 100% chance for a 4-second slow on her last hit reaches all the way to 550 range, wiping UltraBaaBaa right off the stage while Ostromeda and Dread Bore are pinned briefly. Her only weakness here is Lord Gravey, as she is vulnerable to his Knockback.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Amaterasu]]: Amaterasu outranges all of the major threats of the stage while dealing [[Massive Damage]] to everything in her wake, greatly expediting the process of approaching Filibuster. She is also more than capable of taking out UltraBaaBaa's Barrier and permanently putting down Deathshund with her Barrier Breaker and Z-Killer respectively.
*[[Eternal Reika]]: An incredible Zombie and Alien nuker, perfect for quickly taking out every single major threat in this stage. She's able to solo Deathshund, Ostromeda, and Lord Gravey, as she outranges and deals Massive Damage to them. Her niche is similar to Almighty Amaterasu, but without needing to invest in her Talents.
*[[Voli (Uber Rare Cat)|Gigavolta]]: Excellent for stalling Ostromeda as their [[Freeze]] can almost permanently disable it, plus their short cooldown makes them able to be used to pin Filibuster and Ostromeda to the base and sent out again by the time Filibuster attacks to stall Ostromeda at your base after Filibuster is lured.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: An obvious pick, considering she targets the majority of the enemies in the stage. Lunacia's Explosion gives her the ability to snipe Filibuster past supporting enemies through its sheer piercing range, she can snipe Zollows due to the lingering nature of said Explosion, her Freeze against Aliens is great against Ostromeda, and her [[Strong Against]] Zombies makes her a good choice for taking out Deathshund.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Kasa Jizo]]: With his Toxic Immune Talent, can be used to prevent you from losing ground to the Zollow. He's effective at killing the starting Gabriels, and outranges every enemy except Deathshund.

